      "id": "https://www.semanticscholar.org/paper/973ec58e15df38145de8a202bb7f26b8c697abb3",
      "direction_id": "editing-reliability-evaluation",
      "direction_name": "编辑可靠性与行为控制",
      "week": "2026-W22",
      "title": "Reliable Batch-Sequential Model Editing via Enhanced Editing Anchor Compression",
      "title_zh": "《通过增强编辑锚压缩实现可靠的批序式模型编辑》",
      "authors": [
        "Hao Xu",
        "Ziqi Peng",
        "Xiaoyu Wang",
        "Han Guo",
        "Zhenhua Ling"
      ],
      "url": "https://www.semanticscholar.org/paper/973ec58e15df38145de8a202bb7f26b8c697abb3",
      "pdf_url": "",
      "category": "via-citation",
      "published": "",
      "collected": "2026-05-31",
      "abstract": "Large language models (LLMs) often suffer from outdated or incorrect knowledge, prompting ongoing research into efficient model editing. Existing methods, however, mainly target individual knowledge facts. When multiple facts need to be edited in a coherent sequence, they frequently lead to deviations or even breakdowns in model's general abilities. This problem intensifies in batch-sequential editing, where multiple facts are updated simultaneously, compared to single-sequential editing. In this work, by analyzing the parameter matrix, we identify that the degradation stems from unintended modifications that should ideally remain unaffected. These changes accumulate with the number and batch size of edits, ultimately harming editing performance and general abilities. To address this, we propose Batch-Aware Editing Anchor Compression (B-EAC), a framework tailored for sequential model editing. B-EAC dynamically selects essential anchors for each edit while compressing the influence on nearby parameters. It adopts a layer-wise anchor selection strategy to prevent anchor conflicts during concurrent edits and introduces a rolling anchor refresh mechanism to enhance adaptability across batches. Experiments conducted on three LLMs across four tasks demonstrate that B-EAC effectively suppresses deviation during model editing, achieving a 36.54% performance improvement compared to the case without it. Our work offers a practical and theoretically grounded framework for updating LLMs efficiently, paving the way for continual knowledge refinement in real-world applications.",
      "abstract_zh": "大语言模型常携带过时或错误知识，催生了高效模型编辑研究。现有方法多针对单条知识编辑，在批序式批量同时更新多条知识时，易导致模型通用能力偏移甚至崩溃。本文分析发现性能退化源于非目标参数被意外修改，修改随编辑累积损害性能，为此提出批感知编辑锚压缩框架B-EAC，在三个大模型四个任务上实验显示，相对无该方案性能提升36.54%。",
      "has_code": false,
      "repo_url": "",
