      "title": "BAGEN: Are LLM Agents Budget-Aware?",
      "title_zh": "BAGEN：大语言模型智能体具备预算感知能力吗？",
      "authors": [
        "Yuxiang Lin",
        "Zihan Wang",
        "Mengyang Liu",
        "Yuxuan Shan",
        "Longju Bai",
        "Junyao Zhang",
        "Xing Jin",
        "Bo Chen",
        "Jinyan Su",
        "Xingyao Wang",
        "Jiaxin Pei",
        "Manling Li"
      ],
      "url": "http://arxiv.org/abs/2606.00198",
      "pdf_url": "http://arxiv.org/pdf/2606.00198",
      "category": "via-citation",
      "published": "",
      "collected": "2026-06-02",
      "abstract": "While agents are increasingly spending more resources, today agent cost is mostly measured only after execution. A Budget-Aware Agent (BAGEN) should treat budget as an active control signal, rather than a passive cost metric. We first systematically define budget estimation as internal budgets (from agent computation) and external budgets (from agent actions). We then formalize budget-awareness as progressive interval estimation: at each step of a plan, an agent should predict an upper and lower bound on remaining budget, and alert when completion is unlikely. Scoring with a rollout-replay protocol, we find consistent failure patterns on four environments and five frontier agents: (1) strong agents do not necessarily have strong budget-awareness, with correlation r=0.35. (2) frontier models are consistently over-optimistic, continue spending on tasks that are unlikely to succeed, instead of alerting the user early. (3) budget-aware signal is actionable and trainable. Early stop saves 28-64% tokens on failed trajectories, and SFT+RL strengthens early stop and alert behavior. (4) precise interval calibration remains challenging, with interval coverage capping at 47% after SFT+RL. Project page: https://ragen-ai.github.io/bagen/",
      "abstract_zh": "当前智能体消耗的资源不断增长，但现有方案大多仅在执行后统计智能体成本。本文提出将预算作为主动控制信号而非被动成本指标的预算感知智能体BAGEN，将预算分为内部计算预算与外部动作预算，形式化为渐进区间估计，在任务不可能完成时发出警报。评测发现了现有前沿智能体的一致失败模式，SFT+RL可强化提前停止行为，节省28%-64%失败轨迹的token，但区间校准覆盖率最高仅47%。",
      "has_code": false,
      "repo_url": "",
      "repo_stars": 0,
      "hf_upvotes": 0,
      "citation_count": 0,
      "venue": "",
      "venue_year": "",
      "venue_type": "",
      "venue_url": "",
      "venue_confidence": "",
      "venue_source": "",
      "is_authority_venue": false,
      "ingest_source": "",
      "manual_reason": "",
      "manual_tags": [],
      "problem": "现有大语言模型智能体大多仅在执行后统计成本，未将预算作为主动控制信号，易浪费不必要的资源。",
      "method": "将预算分为内部计算预算与外部动作预算，将预算感知形式化为渐进区间估计，用SFT+RL训练强化提前停止警报行为。",
      "contribution": "定义了智能体预算感知问题，系统性评测了现有前沿智能体的预算感知能力，验证了该思路可训练可落地。",
      "limitations": "精确的预算区间校准仍存在挑战，经SFT+RL训练后区间覆盖率最高仅能达到47%。",
      "key_finding": "强智能体能力与预算感知相关性仅r=0.35，前沿模型普遍过度乐观，提前停止可节省28-64%失败轨迹token。",
      "theme": "智能体预算控制",
      "method_family": "agent harness",
      "agent_setting": "通用多步智能体任务",
      "control_mechanism": "将预算作为主动控制信号，通过渐进区间估计预判剩余预算，用SFT+RL训练强化提前停止警报行为。",
      "evaluation_environment": "四类智能体测试环境，采用rollout-replay协议评测，指标含token节省率、区间覆盖率。",
      "evaluation_signal": "评测前沿智能体的预算感知能力，统计token节省比例与预算区间覆盖率，验证提前止损的实际收益。",
      "failure_mode": "智能体预算感知能力不足，普遍过度乐观，在无望完成的任务上持续浪费资源。",
