      "id": "2608.05790",
      "direction_id": "agent-skills-harness",
      "direction_name": "Agent Skills 与 Harness",
      "week": "2026-W33",
      "title": "ChainClaw: A Layered Agent Framework for Reliable On-Chain Execution",
      "title_zh": "ChainClaw：面向可靠链上执行的分层智能体框架",
      "authors": [
        "Jiacheng Wei",
        "Zhaoxin Fan",
        "Xinyang Wen",
        "Yuqin Lan",
        "Dongrun Li",
        "Wenjun Wu",
        "Faguo Wu",
        "Xiao Zhang"
      ],
      "url": "http://arxiv.org/abs/2608.05790",
      "pdf_url": "http://arxiv.org/pdf/2608.05790",
      "category": "via-citation",
      "published": "",
      "collected": "2026-08-15",
      "abstract": "General-purpose large language model agents have achieved strong performance on tool-augmented tasks, yet they rely on assumptions break down in blockchain environments. On-chain execution is stateful, adversarial, and economically irreversible, exposing three fundamental gaps: Reactivity, Irreversibility, and Observability. We propose ChainClaw, a blockchain-native agent framework built on OpenClaw, that addresses all three gaps through a layered architecture comprising an event-driven orchestration layer, a simulation-based safety intelligence layer, and an on-chain monitoring runtime layer, unified by a cross-layer memory subsystem. ChainClaw closes the Reactivity gap via event ingestion and simulation feedback, the Irreversibility gap via a pre-execution safety pipeline with transaction simulation and action guard, and the Observability gap via an on-chain read adapter and transaction monitor. We evaluate ChainClaw on a purpose-built benchmark covering seven tasks across four categories and five dimensions. ChainClaw consistently outperforms representative baselines on both safety and task completion.",
      "abstract_zh": "通用大语言模型智能体在工具增强任务上已取得出色性能，但其依赖的假设在区块链环境中不成立。链上执行具有有状态、对抗性和经济不可逆性，存在响应性、不可逆性、可观测性三大核心缺口。本文提出基于OpenClaw构建的区块链原生智能体框架ChainClaw，通过分层架构加跨层内存子系统解决三大缺口，评测显示其性能优于代表性基线。",
      "has_code": false,
      "repo_url": "",
      "repo_stars": 0,
      "hf_upvotes": 0,
      "citation_count": 0,
      "venue": "",
      "venue_year": "",
      "venue_type": "",
      "venue_url": "",
      "venue_confidence": "",
      "venue_source": "",
      "is_authority_venue": false,
      "ingest_source": "",
      "manual_reason": "",
      "manual_tags": [],
      "problem": "通用大语言模型智能体的假设不适配区块链环境，链上执行存在响应性、不可逆性、可观测性三大核心缺口。",
      "method": "提出区块链原生分层智能体框架ChainClaw，通过三层架构加跨层内存子系统解决链上执行三大缺口。",
      "contribution": "构建了专用评测基准，ChainClaw在安全性和任务完成度上均持续优于代表性基线方法。",
      "limitations": "摘要未提及",
      "key_finding": "带预执行安全管道的分层架构，可有效提升链上智能体的安全性与任务完成率，性能优于现有代表性方法。",
      "theme": "链上智能体框架",
      "method_family": "agent harness",
      "agent_setting": "链上/tool-use",
      "control_mechanism": "通过分层架构设计，加入预执行安全模拟与动作防护、链上运行监控，保障链上智能体执行的可靠性。",
      "evaluation_environment": "自定义专用基准，涵盖四类七任务五维度，评测指标为安全性与任务完成率",
      "evaluation_signal": "在自建多维度链上执行基准中，ChainClaw在安全性和任务完成率两项指标上均持续优于代表性基线。",
      "failure_mode": "通用大模型智能体链上执行存在响应不足、不可逆风险高、可观测性差",
