      "url": "http://arxiv.org/abs/2608.30300v1",
      "pdf_url": "https://arxiv.org/pdf/2608.30300v1",
      "category": "cs.SE",
      "published": "2026-08-31 06:13:51+00:00",
      "collected": "2026-09-01",
      "abstract": "Modern software systems rely heavily on third-party dependencies, but upgrading those dependencies remains a costly maintenance activity. Dependency upgrades do not always preserve the function signatures, type systems, APIs, or runtime semantics assumed by existing code. Consequently, developers often need to perform source code adaptations to accommodate dependency-induced changes. However, such code-level changes are often not explicitly communicated to project maintainers, posing a significant challenge to software reliability.   Meanwhile, coding agents have emerged as a new form of software development tool and are increasingly adopted by developers due to their automation capabilities. In this paper, we introduce DEPBENCH, a benchmark consisting of 203 real-world dependency-upgrade tasks across five package ecosystems spanning five language communities, each involving hidden code-level changes that require source code adaptation. We evaluate mainstream coding agents on DEPBENCH. The best completed configuration solves only 104/203 tasks (51.2%), with substantial variation across agent harnesses, models, and ecosystems, highlighting an important gap between current agent capabilities and real-world software maintenance needs.",
      "abstract_zh": "现代软件高度依赖第三方依赖，依赖升级常改变原有代码依赖的API、语义等要素，隐式变化需要开发者适配代码，给软件可靠性带来挑战。本文构建DEPBENCH基准，包含203个真实依赖升级任务，评测发现最优编码Agent仅解决51.2%的任务，能力与实际需求存在缺口。",
