      "title": "S-DAG: A Subject-Based Directed Acyclic Graph for Multi-Agent Heterogeneous Reasoning",
      "title_zh": "S-DAG：面向多智能体异质推理的基于主题的有向无环图",
      "authors": [
        "Jiangwen Dong",
        "Zehui Lin",
        "Wanyu Lin",
        "Mingjin Zhang"
      ],
      "url": "http://arxiv.org/abs/2511.06727",
      "pdf_url": "http://arxiv.org/pdf/2511.06727",
      "category": "via-citation",
      "published": "",
      "collected": "2026-06-08",
      "abstract": "Large Language Models (LLMs) have achieved impressive performance in complex reasoning problems. Their effectiveness highly depends on the specific nature of the task, especially the required domain knowledge. Existing approaches, such as mixture-of-experts, typically operate at the task level; they are too coarse to effectively solve the heterogeneous problems involving multiple subjects. This work proposes a novel framework that performs fine-grained analysis at subject level equipped with a designated multi-agent collaboration strategy for addressing heterogeneous problem reasoning. Specifically, given an input query, we first employ a Graph Neural Network to identify the relevant subjects and infer their interdependencies to generate an Subject-based Directed Acyclic Graph (S-DAG), where nodes represent subjects and edges encode information flow. Then we profile the LLM models by assigning each model a subject-specific expertise score, and select the top-performing one for matching corresponding subject of the S-DAG. Such subject-model matching enables graph-structured multi-agent collaboration where information flows from the starting model to the ending model over S-DAG. We curate and release multi-subject subsets of standard benchmarks (MMLU-Pro, GPQA, MedMCQA) to better reflect complex, real-world reasoning tasks. Extensive experiments show that our approach significantly outperforms existing task-level model selection and multi-agent collaboration baselines in accuracy and efficiency. These results highlight the effectiveness of subject-aware reasoning and structured collaboration in addressing complex and multi-subject problems.",
      "abstract_zh": "大语言模型在复杂推理任务上表现出色，但其效果高度依赖任务领域知识，现有混合专家等方法多在任务层面操作，粒度较粗，难以有效解决涉及多个主题的异质问题。本文提出细粒度主题层面分析的新框架，搭配专门设计的多智能体协作策略，先构建S-DAG刻画主题依赖，再按主题专长匹配模型，实现图结构多智能体协作，还发布了多主题基准子集，实验证明该方法准确率和效率显著优于现有基线。",
      "has_code": false,
      "repo_url": "",
      "repo_stars": 0,
      "hf_upvotes": 0,
      "citation_count": 4,
      "venue": "AAAI",
      "venue_year": 2025,
      "venue_type": "conference",
      "venue_url": "https://www.semanticscholar.org/paper/6ab1a00d1785fbe9c04ea37d36355a4f7ebfe6b3",
      "venue_confidence": "semantic-scholar",
      "venue_source": "semantic-scholar",
      "is_authority_venue": true,
      "ingest_source": "",
      "manual_reason": "",
      "manual_tags": [],
      "problem": "现有大语言模型多主题异质推理方法多为任务级粒度，粒度过粗，无法有效处理跨主题的复杂异质推理问题。",
      "method": "构建主题级有向无环图S-DAG刻画主题依赖，为每个主题匹配对应专长的大语言模型，实现图结构多智能体协作推理。",
      "contribution": "提出主题感知的S-DAG多智能体协作推理框架，发布多主题基准子集，实验验证效果优于现有任务级方法。",
