      "direction_name": "多 Agent 交互与一致性",
      "week": "2026-W35",
      "title": "Towards Traffic Modelling of Multi-Agent Systems: The Role of Coordination Topology",
      "title_zh": "面向多智能体系统的流量建模：协调拓扑的作用",
      "authors": [
        "Davide Lamagna",
        "Albert Cabellos",
        "Alberto Rodriguez-Natal",
        "Gábor Rétvári",
        "Berta Serracanta"
      ],
      "url": "http://arxiv.org/abs/2608.20494v1",
      "pdf_url": "https://arxiv.org/pdf/2608.20494v1",
      "category": "cs.NI",
      "published": "2026-08-20 18:30:46+00:00",
      "collected": "2026-08-24",
      "abstract": "Multi-agent LLM systems are an emerging networked workload whose rapid deployment raises questions about the traffic patterns they generate. Compared to conventional applications, these systems generate requests internally: a single user task can induce a structured sequence of model calls whose timing is governed by coordination logic rather than by user arrival rate. It is not clear whether classical traffic models, designed for human-driven workloads, apply to this setting.   We present an empirical characterisation of LLM-call interarrival time distributions across sequential, star, and full-mesh agentic coordination topologies, using a multi-layer measurement framework over 500 repeated runs per topology. We find that topology fundamentally shapes the arrival process of requests to the LLM backend: fan-out coordination introduces a structural bimodality absent in sequential execution, and the reasoningphase component is best described by a log-normal distribution, with the Poisson exponential null model decisively rejected across all topologies. These differences propagate to inference and network level metrics. The framework and analysis pipeline are released openly at https://github.com/dlamagna/agentraffic.",
      "abstract_zh": "多智能体大语言模型系统是新兴的网络化工作负载，其快速部署催生了对其所生成流量模式的研究问题。与传统应用不同，这类系统会内部生成请求：单个用户任务可产生结构化模型调用序列，调用时序由协调逻辑而非用户到达率决定，面向人类驱动工作负载的经典流量模型是否适用于该场景尚不明确。本文针对三种协调拓扑开展实证分析，每个拓扑重复运行500次，开源了所提出的分析框架。",
      "has_code": true,
