      "id": "2608.28264",
      "direction_id": "multi-agent-consistency",
      "direction_name": "多 Agent 交互与一致性",
      "week": "2026-W36",
      "title": "Finding Where the Buck Stops: An Automated Failure Attribution-Based Reflection Framework for Multi-Agent Collaboration",
      "title_zh": "找到责任源头：基于自动故障归因的多智能体协作反思框架",
      "authors": [
        "Xiaoqing Wang",
        "Keman Huang",
        "Bin Liang",
        "Hongyu Li",
        "Xiaoyong Du",
        "Wuqiong Pan"
      ],
      "url": "http://arxiv.org/abs/2608.28264v1",
      "pdf_url": "https://arxiv.org/pdf/2608.28264v1",
      "category": "cs.AI",
      "published": "2026-08-28 12:26:03+00:00",
      "collected": "2026-08-31",
      "abstract": "Multi-agent systems (MAS) powered by large language models have shown promise for complex tasks but suffer from high failure rates. Current self-reflection methods for MAS require all agents to reflect upon failure, overlooking a critical reality: failures typically stem from a specific agent leading the task astray, namely the decisive error agent, while others merely fulfill their regular duties. Forcing regular-behaving agents to reflect contaminates their memory with wrong insights. Hence, we propose DoCtOR (Diagnose-then-Correct PPO-enhanced Reflection), a novel reflection framework that enhances multi-agent collaboration. DoCtOR first identifies the decisive error step and decisive error agent through automated failure attribution, then employs counterfactual reasoning to generate a corrected decisive error step, and finally engages only the decisive error agent to produce targeted reflections. Experimental results show DoCtOR achieves 22%, 26%, and 27% improvements over initial success rates on HotPotQA, ChartQAPro, and Mind2Web datasets, outperforming Reflexion, Retroformer, and COPPER. We further establish the generalizability of our diagnose-then-correct paradigm and demonstrate that in low-resource settings, focusing reflection on reasoning steps after the decisive error step achieves comparable quality to reflecting on the complete failure trajectory.",
      "abstract_zh": "大语言模型驱动的多智能体系统在复杂任务中具备潜力但失败率较高，现有多智能体自反思方法要求所有智能体参与失败反思，忽略了失败通常源自特定决定性错误智能体，强制正常智能体反思会用错误见解污染其记忆。本文提出DoCtOR（诊断后矫正的PPO增强反思框架），先定位错误步骤与错误智能体，仅让目标智能体做针对性反思，实验在三个数据集上初始成功率提升22%、26%、27%，优于多个基线。",
      "has_code": false,
      "repo_url": "",
      "repo_stars": 0,
      "hf_upvotes": 0,
      "citation_count": 0,
      "venue": "",
      "venue_year": "",
      "venue_type": "",
      "venue_url": "",
      "venue_confidence": "",
      "venue_source": "",
      "is_authority_venue": false,
      "ingest_source": "",
      "manual_reason": "",
      "manual_tags": [],
      "problem": "现有多智能体自反思要求所有智能体参与失败反思，错误见解会污染正常智能体记忆，未能针对错误源头改进。",
      "method": "提出DoCtOR反思框架，通过自动故障归因定位错误步骤与错误智能体，仅让错误智能体做针对性反思。",
      "contribution": "提出诊断后矫正的反思范式，在三个基准数据集上成功率提升显著，效果优于多个现有基线方法。",
      "limitations": "摘要未提及",
      "key_finding": "仅针对定位出的决定性错误智能体做反思，可在三个数据集上将初始成功率分别提升22%、26%、27%。",
      "theme": "多智能体协作反思",
      "method_family": "multi-agent coordination",
      "agent_setting": "multi-agent QA web",
      "control_mechanism": "通过自动故障归因定位出错智能体，仅要求出错智能体做针对性反思，避免错误污染正常智能体记忆。",
      "evaluation_environment": "HotPotQA、ChartQAPro、Mind2Web，评测指标为任务初始成功率",
      "evaluation_signal": "在三个基准数据集上，初始成功率相比基线分别提升22%、26%、27%，低资源设置下仍能保持良好性能。",
      "failure_mode": "全智能体反思模式下，正常智能体记忆会被错误见解污染，失败无法得到针对性修正。",
