      "abstract": "Deceptive controls can redirect a web agent while remaining visually valid and clickable. DebateGuard is a parameter-free protocol that reviews each proposed action. A Navigator selects a task-directed operation, an Auditor checks the target and likely consequence, and an independent Judge authorizes execution or requests a revision. A fixed round budget bounds each browser step and preserves its decision record. Across four RUC domains and several vision–language agent pairings, DebateGuard raises task success and reduces deception-triggered failures without updating the participating models.",
