      "id": "2606.05464",
      "direction_id": "agent-policy-optimization",
      "direction_name": "Agent 策略优化与在线蒸馏",
      "week": "2026-W23",
      "title": "Step-by-Step Optimization-like Reasoning in LLMs over Expanding Search Spaces",
      "title_zh": "大语言模型在扩展搜索空间下的类优化分步推理",
      "authors": [
        "Nicolás Astorga",
        "Nabeel Seedat",
        "Mihaela van der Schaar"
      ],
      "url": "http://arxiv.org/abs/2606.05464v1",
      "pdf_url": "https://arxiv.org/pdf/2606.05464v1",
      "category": "cs.AI",
      "published": "2026-06-03 21:43:38+00:00",
      "collected": "2026-06-06",
      "abstract": "Verifiable reward training has improved mathematical and coding reasoning, but these domains capture only part of step-by-step decision making. Many real-world tasks require finding a high-value feasible plan among many valid alternatives. We introduce OPT*, a scalable family of optimization-style tasks for training and evaluating LLM step-by-step optimization-like reasoning along a complexity axis: each task provides a feasibility checker and evaluator, while a complexity parameter expands the search space without requiring new human labels. This motivates studying these tasks in two regimes: (i) solver-guided online policy optimization, which uses a solver as a value oracle for partial states and applies rank-based reward shaping to reinforce better next steps, and (ii) search-based offline RL when such solvers are unavailable. Theoretically, we relate success in large search spaces to the information a reasoner extracts per unit of search budget. Empirically, we ablate the ingredients that make search efficient on OPT* and show that training on OPT* improves step-by-step optimization-like reasoning.",
      "abstract_zh": "可验证奖励训练已提升大语言模型的数学与编码推理，但这些领域仅覆盖分步决策的一部分，诸多现实任务需要在大量有效候选中寻找高价值可行方案。本文提出可扩展的类优化任务族OPT*，任务自带可行性检查器与评估器，可通过复杂度参数扩展搜索空间，无需新增人工标注。作者分两种场景开展研究，提出求解器引导的在线策略优化与无求解器的搜索式离线RL，从理论和实验验证了方法有效性。",
      "has_code": false,
      "repo_url": "",
      "repo_stars": 0,
      "hf_upvotes": 0,
      "citation_count": 0,
      "venue": "",
      "venue_year": "",
      "venue_type": "",
      "venue_url": "",
      "venue_confidence": "",
      "venue_source": "",
      "is_authority_venue": false,
      "ingest_source": "",
      "manual_reason": "",
      "manual_tags": [],
      "problem": "现有可验证奖励推理研究多局限于数学编码领域，缺乏针对大搜索空间下分步优化决策任务的研究。",
      "method": "提出可扩展类优化任务族OPT*，分场景设计求解器引导的在线策略优化与无求解器的搜索式离线强化学习。",
      "contribution": "提出新任务族OPT*，理论关联推理效果与搜索信息效率，实验证明OPT*训练可提升大模型类优化推理能力。",
      "limitations": "摘要未提及",
      "key_finding": "通过消融实验验证了OPT*任务各组件对搜索效率的提升作用，在OPT*上训练可稳定改进大模型的类优化分步推理。",
      "theme": "在线策略优化",
      "method_family": "policy optimization",
      "agent_setting": "search",
      "control_mechanism": "以求解器作为偏序状态的值预言机，采用基于排名的奖励塑形强化更好的分步决策，依托新基准训练评估模型。",
      "evaluation_environment": "OPT*任务基准",
      "evaluation_signal": "验证OPT*各组件对搜索效率的提升效果，以及OPT*训练对大语言模型类优化推理能力的改进作用。",
      "failure_mode": "摘要未提及",
      "reliability_risk": "新基准未在真实任务中验证泛化性，无求解器场景的效果缺乏充分的实验验证。",
