      "week": "2026-W31",
      "title": "Cybersecurity Detection Classification with Reasoning-enabled Language Models",
      "title_zh": "基于推理增强大语言模型的网络安全检测分类",
      "authors": [
        "Amol Khanna",
        "Manu Nandan",
        "Cristian Viorel Popa",
        "Joan Pujol-Roig",
        "Diana Bolocan",
        "Laura Vasilie",
        "Alexandru Apostu",
        "Chase Helwig",
        "Mihaela Gaman",
        "Michael Brautbar",
        "Edward Raff",
        "Chase Midler",
        "Sven Krasser"
      ],
      "url": "http://arxiv.org/abs/2607.28460v1",
      "pdf_url": "https://arxiv.org/pdf/2607.28460v1",
      "category": "cs.LG",
      "published": "2026-07-30 16:22:13+00:00",
      "collected": "2026-07-31",
      "abstract": "A major issue in Security Operations Centers (SOCs) is alert fatigue, as the number of detections reported is more than staff can triage in a given day. Prior work prompts or fine-tunes large language models (LLMs) to emit a triage label directly, but does not train them to reason about whether a detection is a genuine threat. We train a chain-of-thought (CoT) reasoning-enabled triage classifier on real, human-labeled Windows endpoint detections by combining automated prompt optimization, self-training, and reinforcement learning with verifiable rewards. We find that CoT reasoning also degrades the label-token probabilities that automated triage relies on, so we separately train a calibrator that reads the full reasoning trace and estimates the probability that the verdict is correct. Our system reaches 82.6% test accuracy and, at the high-confidence operating point that governs automated triage, improves benign recall by 43.0% and malicious recall by 18.3% over a direct-label LLM classifier. We further show that the trained calibrator is necessary - an untrained confidence judge collapses high-confidence recall to zero - and that a finetuned 30B model significantly outperforms frontier general-purpose models, motivating targeted training over scale.",
      "abstract_zh": "安全运营中心（SOC）面临严重告警疲劳问题，每日生成的检测量远超人工排查能力。已有工作仅提示或微调大语言模型直接输出分诊标签，未训练模型推理检测是否为真实威胁。本文结合自动提示优化、自训练与可验证奖励强化学习，在人工标注的Windows端点检测数据上训练了支持思维链推理的分诊分类器，针对CoT推理会降低标签概率质量的问题额外训练校准器，实验证明系统性能显著优于基线方法。",
      "has_code": false,
      "repo_url": "",
      "repo_stars": 0,
      "hf_upvotes": 0,
      "citation_count": 0,
      "venue": "",
      "venue_year": "",
      "venue_type": "",
      "venue_url": "",
      "venue_confidence": "",
      "venue_source": "",
      "is_authority_venue": false,
      "ingest_source": "",
      "manual_reason": "",
      "manual_tags": [],
      "problem": "安全运营中心存在告警疲劳问题，现有大语言模型分诊方法未训练推理能力，CoT推理会损害标签概率质量。",
      "method": "结合自动提示优化、自训练与可验证奖励强化学习训练CoT分诊分类器，额外训练校准器估计判决置信度。",
      "contribution": "提出的系统测试准确率达82.6%，大幅提升自动分诊召回率，验证领域针对性训练优于通用大模型扩参。",
      "limitations": "摘要未提及",
      "key_finding": "CoT推理会降低标签token概率，未训练的置信度评判器会使高置信度召回降至零，微调30B领域模型优于前沿通用大模型。",
      "theme": "网络安全检测分类",
      "method_family": "reward learning",
      "agent_setting": "非Agent论文",
      "control_mechanism": "通过带可验证奖励的强化学习训练推理增强分类器，额外训练校准器改进判决置信度估计，提升分类性能。",
      "evaluation_environment": "真实Windows端点网络安全检测任务，评测指标为测试准确率、召回率",
      "evaluation_signal": "系统测试准确率达82.6%，高置信工作点良性召回提升43.0%、恶意召回提升18.3%，性能优于所有对比基线。",
      "failure_mode": "现有分诊大模型无推理能力，CoT推理降低标签概率，未训练置信器会导致高置信召回归零",
      "reliability_risk": "依赖人工标注领域数据，30B大模型推理部署成本较高，工业落地存在一定成本压力。",
      "industrial_relevance": "high",
      "read_priority": "medium",
